A Docker image is not a single file, but a set of layers stored by Docker, usually as compressed files and metadata. You cannot simply open it like a regular file, but you can inspect its contents.

To see the contents of a Docker image, you can:

Create a container from the image (without running it):
docker create --name temp_redis redis:latest

Copy files from the container to your host:
docker cp temp_redis:/path/in/container /path/on/host

Or, start a shell inside the container:
docker run -it --rm redis:latest sh

This lets you browse the filesystem inside the image.